                                "sense_id": "d1a75aeb-eecd-35a9-9782-5a49f09ab654",
                                "text": "1973, Lennaert Nijgh, \"Jan Klaassen de trompetter\", performed by Rob de Nijs, In de uren van de middag.\nJan Klaassen was trompetter in het leger van de prins / Hij marcheerde van Den Helder tot Den Briel / Hij had geen geld en hij was geen held en hij hield niet van het krijgsgeweld / Maar trompetter was hij wel in hart en ziel",
                                "translation": "Jan Klaassen was a trumpet player in the Prince's army [= Prince of Orange] / He marched from Den Helder to Den Briel / He had no money and he was no hero and he did not like the thick of war / But yes, he was a trumpet player in his heart and in his soul",
                                "english": "Jan Klaassen was a trumpet player in the Prince's army [= Prince of Orange] / He marched from Den Helder to Den Briel / He had no money and he was no hero and he did not like the thick of war / But yes, he was a trumpet player in his heart and in his soul"
                            }
                        ]
